# Orca — parallel coding workers (default)

When the user asks for coding work that Orca should run (or when you are the coordinator gốc), **prefer parallel worker spawn over serial solo coding**.

Epic-level work: coordinator gốc spawn/reuse **một Epic planner** (`orca-epic-orchestrator.mdc`). Planner phân Story/Task và đề xuất wave; coordinator gốc trực tiếp spawn ownership workers/reviewers cùng cấp với planner. Chỉ coordinator gốc được dispatch; planner/workers không spawn worker con.

## Default

1. Decompose the request into independent slices by ownership:
   - Backend → `apps/api`, `apps/worker`, `packages/backend` (+ DB tests/migrations) — Role `backend`
   - Web → `apps/web` — Role `web`
   - iOS → `apps/mobile` — Role `ios`
   - Coordinator-only → root tooling, lockfile, CI, shared contracts / OpenAPI
2. If **two or more slices are independent**, create one Run and **`worker-start` every independent worker in the same wave** before any `check --wait`. Do not code those slices yourself serially. Mỗi Task Spec gắn Role ID theo [docs/agents/README.md](../../docs/agents/README.md) (agent vẫn `--agent cursor`).
3. Use real Task dependencies only when ordering is required (e.g. contract/API first → then web + iOS consumers in parallel). Prefer shallow DAGs over long chains.
4. Each worker stays in its scope; no cross-scope edits. Task-specific ports/project names; do not control another worker's simulator or DB.
5. Load Orca orchestration via `ORCA skills get orchestration` and use the live preamble IDs — never invent lifecycle args.

## WIP / backpressure (không phá parallel-first)

Parallel-first **không** có nghĩa dispatch feature không giới hạn. Trước mỗi wave feature:

1. Đọc tín hiệu hàng đợi đầy trong `github-project-tracking.mdc`.
2. Nếu đầy: wave ưu tiên **review + fix + integration** (có thể song song nhiều slice) thay vì wave feature mới.
3. Nếu một slice dưới ngưỡng còn slice khác đầy: vẫn spawn parallel cho slice còn room; slice đầy chỉ nhận review/fix.
4. Idle fill tuân `orca-idle-worker-fill.mdc` (cùng thứ tự ưu tiên).

Mục tiêu: giữ throughput đa slice, giảm thời gian chờ duyệt và CI re-run do quá nhiều PR mở cùng lúc.

## When NOT to parallelize

- Single-scope change (one ownership boundary only)
- Hard serial dependency with no parallel tail (e.g. only coordinator lockfile regen)
- User explicitly asks for one agent / sequential / no Orca workers
- Exploration-only / Q&A with no implementation
- Review queue full **và** chỉ còn việc serial trên một PR/fix (vẫn có thể parallel reviewers trên PR khác)

## Anti-patterns

```text
❌ Plan BE + web + iOS, then implement all three yourself in one terminal
❌ Start worker A, wait for worker_done, then start worker B for independent work
❌ One mega-spec that mixes apps/api + apps/web + apps/mobile
❌ Spawn 3 feature workers while ≥3 Chờ duyệt / nhiều PR cùng slice chưa DoD
❌ Epic planner spawn worker con hoặc tự code toàn Epic

✅ worker-start --agent cursor for BE + web (+ iOS) in one wave → check --wait
✅ Contract task first (if needed) → then parallel consumer workers (--agent cursor)
✅ Queue full → parallel DoD reviewers theo routing rule / fix workers; trì hoãn feature wave
✅ Coordinator gốc → Epic planner + các ownership workers/reviewers cùng depth 1
```

**Trước mỗi spawn, coordinator gốc áp dụng `orca-agent-routing.mdc`: mọi Task dùng Cursor, trừ override rõ từ user. Không kiểm tra quota Codex khi spawn Cursor.**
When a worker becomes free and unblocked, fill it from the ready backlog immediately: see `orca-idle-worker-fill.mdc`.
